Sources of Statistical Errors
The statistical errors may arise from the following sources:
• Errors of Origin: Error of origin arises due to lack of proper definition of the subject- matter, bias of
investigator, defective questionnaire, improper sampling, or the inherent instability of collected data.
Error of Manipulation: These errors arise due to manipulation in counting, measurement, description and
approximation of the various figures.
Error of Inadequacy: It may arise due to use of incomplete or unrepresentative data or due to
irresponsible/careless/ unqualified investigators.
Error of Interpretation: Such errors can be made when data is misinterpreted.
