Important Published
Official Publications of Central and State Governments: The publications by Indian
Government are Annual Economic Survey, Documents of Five-Year Plans, IndiaAnnual Book, Census, etc. regarding important economic variables like national
income, saving, investment, employment, etc.
Semi-Government Publications: Semi-Government organisations like municipalities,
District Boards and others also publish reports in respect of birth, death, education,
sanitation and many other related fields.
International Publications: Certain International institutions publish reports from
time to time regarding economic matters which are of great significance. These
reports are regularly published by the agencies like United Nations Organisation
(UNO), World Health Organisation (WHO), International Monetary Fund (IMF), etc.
Publications of Trade Associations: Some big trade associations like Institute of
Chartered Accountants, Trade Unions, etc. publish data collected through their
statistical and research divisions.
Newspapers and Magazines: Various newspapers as well as magazines also collect
data in respect of many social and economic aspects. Some of them are Economic
Times, Financial Express, Outlook Money, Business Today, etc.
